- Route DTO numeric-key grammar continuation: expanded direct pinned Fastjson inputs from 339 to 360. `brokerAddrs` and `currIdMap` accept unquoted signed integers, leading-zero integers, plus-signed integers, fractions, negative fractions, and exponent forms with Java Long/Integer coercion. `filterServerTable` and `topicQueueMappingByBroker` accept unquoted numeric keys and use Java number text (`+1` -> `1`, `1e2` -> `100.0`); root bean numeric property keys reject, while ignored nested objects and object-to-String route values accept numeric map keys. The first differential failed on `+1` because the old key scanner handled only signed integers; follow-ups also exposed root-key over-acceptance, string-map key canonicalization, and Fastjson's unquoted numeric keys when stringifying a JSONObject. The route parser now tracks bean/map/array context and applies type-specific key conversion; common Fastjson object-to-String conversion emits numeric JSONObject keys in Java form. All 360 inputs pass. `route.json` SHA-256 `e0a36ac2b1139acacd11536ba9a22bc3532d4b200ec8eabb21b1d0f6a82995e4`.
- Focused route differential and full workspace/all-target tests pass (core 94, protocol 80, remoting 78 unit/6 codec/82 transport, all integration targets); strict all-target/all-feature Clippy passes. Pinned offline Maven verify exits 0 with 22 scenarios, fixture drift and Java cross-decodes; comparator self-test, manifest22, `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, and `git diff --check` pass. The sandboxed workspace-test attempt blocked three loopback binds; rerunning with local socket access passed.
- Updated ADR-0014 and current Phase 6 API/config, route, inventory, and requirement-audit evidence. This closes only the recorded numeric map-key forms and nested object stringification. Other DTO/raw/enum inputs, broader Fastjson grammar, platform settings paths, and final source/API/branch/reverse-export reconciliation remain open. No plan files changed; P6-V04 stays `PENDING_PHASE_19`.
